---
title: Rosemary-Rubbed Duck Breast with Caramelized Apricots
source: http://www.myrecipes.com/recipe/rosemary-rubbed-duck-breast-with-caramelized-apricots-10000000226625/
tags: Duck
---

Combine the @rosemary{3%tbsp}(fresh, chopped), @brown sugar{2%tbsp}, @black pepper{1%tbsp}, and @salt{2%tsp}.

Rub the rosemary mixture over the @duck breasts{12%oz}(skinned and halved).
Cover and chill ~{2%hours}.

Rinse duck with cold water; pat dry.
The skin must be dry to ensure an even sear in the pan.

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #large nonstick skillet{} over medium-high heat.
Add duck, and cook for ~{5%minutes} on each side or until cooked to medium or medium-well.
Remove from pan; let stand for ~{10%minutes}.

Combine the @sugar{1/2%cup} and @white wine vinegar{1/2%cup} in a #small saucepan{}, and bring to a boil.
Cook until thick and amber-colored, about ~{5%minutes}.

Add @apricots{5}(quartered); reduce heat, and cook for ~{1%minute} or until the apricots begin to soften.

> If fresh whole apricots are not available, use canned apricots in the lightest (least syrupy) sauce possible.

Cut duck diagonally across the grain into slices. Serve with caramelized apricots.
